From 05e32057a92cdca847c77ba0ba9f325cad8fae6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:59:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] badgeui: edit a saved card's dump in Write
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cards › a card › options › Edit in Write writes the dump as text next to
it (hf-...-dump.txt: one block per line in hex, the block number and what
it holds as a # comment, sector lines for MIFARE Classic) and opens it in
Write. When Write closes, the text is read back: every block must have
its bytes (MIFARE Classic 16, iCLASS 8, other dumps 16 a row), else
nothing is written and the notice names the line; the text then stays
and opens again, newer than the dump. A good text replaces the .bin
(written beside it, then renamed) and the notice says how many blocks
changed. Dumps over the view's 4 KB are refused rather than cut. The
client's .json beside the dump is left as it was.

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 13/13 on the host (new test_edit_dump_in_write:
an edit, a wrong line kept and fixed, no changes; a MIFARE Classic dump
reads back unchanged). Not yet on the badge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
